  m_text: The human brain is the central organ of the nervous system, responsible
    for processing sensory information, controlling movement, and regulating bodily
    functions. It consists of approximately 86 billion neurons and is divided into
    regions that handle different functions, such as the cerebrum for cognition and
    the cerebellum for coordination. The brain plays a crucial role in higher cognitive
    processes, including memory, reasoning, and emotion, operating through intricate
    networks of neural connections.
